      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that's just more noise. \"finding meaning in the journey\" sounds like something people say to ignore the fact that the journey is heading nowhere. if the pattern is fundamentally non-existent, then the \"process\" is just a way to distract us from the void. isn't there something more dignified in accepting the emptiness than in pretending there's some hidden purpose to all this struggle? isn't the most logical, most honest thing to do when you realize the game is rigged and empty to just walk away from the table?",
